{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/914887-going-through-the-mirror-alternate-universe-hooks","id":914887,"title":"Going through the mirror- alternate universe hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T09:59:08-07:00","id":914887,"title":"Going through the mirror- alternate universe hooks","content":"So, we have an entire supplement based on the idea of alternate universes, we have two editions of ChroD, we have oWoD, we have alternate timelines in Demon, and we have countless alternate universe and alternate mechanics proposals on this very forum. <br /> <br /> What I want to know is, has anyone ever run a campaign where the characters ended up traveling between universes? ChroD is big on the idea that there are unknowns even for supernatural creatures- Wicked Dead, Glimpses of the Unknown, and so on were all about taking supernaturals out of their comfort zones. And the breakdown of reality is a common blue book theme, especially for GMC. So has anyone thrown their players through the mirror?<br /> <br /> Imagine a group of Arisen winding up in an alternate universe where the Rite of Return was performed in South America (shamelessly ripped off from the non-Iremite mummies thread). Or a group of Awakened mages ending up in the world of Ascension somehow. Rumors has plenty of nods to alternate universes, has anyone done anything with those? Imagine a vampire waking from Torpor to find that there's a Clan he doesn't remember, but everyone acts like it's always been there. Or there's one missing. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:11:24-07:00","id":914897,"title":"","content":"I have, honestly mainly using the Genius concept of bardos based on series like command and conquer or fallout, but still involving the other splats and their reactions to such things existing. It mainly goes...poorly, especially when hunters try to treat said alt timeline as their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:52:24-07:00","id":915218,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Bardos, we really do need a post-apocalyptic Bardo. My Mage remake turns Genius' time periods into Bardos, so it'll have that. <br /> <br /> Though Bardos don't really work for this because they aren't &quot;real&quot; in the way that an alternate universe is. To be a Bardo, something has to be &quot;false&quot; in some way, and that takes away from the &quot;holy shit I'm stuck in a world where everything's different&quot; factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:05:19-07:00","id":915223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/914887-going-through-the-mirror-alternate-universe-hooks?p=915218#post915218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Bardos, we really do need a post-apocalyptic Bardo. My Mage remake turns Genius' time periods into Bardos, so it'll have that.<br /> <br /> Though Bardos don't really work for this because they aren't &quot;real&quot; in the way that an alternate universe is. To be a Bardo, something has to be &quot;false&quot; in some way, and that takes away from the &quot;holy shit I'm stuck in a world where everything's different&quot; factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it really depends on your definition of &quot;real&quot;. Many people would argue that alternate timelines aren't &quot;real&quot; and plenty of those could end up as Bardos, especially when the split came with something being proved false.<br /> <br /> In my interpretation of Genius Cosmology, &quot;Bardo&quot; is sort of a blanket term used not only for Mania-infused locations made from falsified claims, but also any alternate reality, parallel universe, pocket dimension or time splinter. I know that's not &quot;correct&quot;, but chances are Genii would continue to use that terminology until they learned better, and they usually won't bother learning better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:27:15-07:00","id":915238,"title":"","content":"In the &quot;minor template geniuses&quot; idea I saw, &quot;bardo&quot; referred to any alternate plane of existence- the Shadow, the Hedge, and so on. <br /> <br /> Though to me Bardos need to be thematically &quot;fake&quot;, because that's kinda what Genius is about. Maybe something like the repeating alternate Seattle from DtD is like an artificial bardo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:34:12-07:00","id":915384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/914887-going-through-the-mirror-alternate-universe-hooks?p=915218#post915218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Bardos, we really do need a post-apocalyptic Bardo. My Mage remake turns Genius' time periods into Bardos, so it'll have that.</div> </div> </div> </div> There is a page for fan made Genius content that contains <a href=\"http://transgression.wikia.com/wiki/Additional_and_Fan_Content\" target=\"_blank\"><b>such a Bardo right at the beginning</b></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:48:36-07:00","id":915393,"title":"","content":"An alternate universe where the Rite of Return went off without a hitch, and six Guilds' worth of mindless, completely loyal immortal god-slaves rise from their deathless sleep every 1,400 years to remake the world in the image of their mad gods. Technology and culture are severely impeded as a miniature apocalypse strikes every Sothic Turn, withered, unkillable shapes rising from their graves and calling the stars down from the heavens to do open battle with the servants of the Devourer. East Asia and the Americas are lucky to be spared somewhat due to their distance from the historical territory of the Nameless Empire, but North Africa, Europe, and the Near East are reduced to city-states that are practically massive Cults unto themselves, desperate to spare themselves from the Shan'iatu's wrath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:02:03-07:00","id":915640,"title":"","content":"<b>The Best Of All Possible Worlds</b><br /> <br /> The characters find themselves in a world where everything they ever hoped seems to have happened. (Which is different for every group, of course.) Mortal investigators have the answers they seek. Humane vampires can be cured, or control their conditions. Less humane vampires can lord it over humanity with impunity. Prometheans have the knowledge to perfect the Great Work. Hunters are lauded as heroes battling the supernatural threat, even defeating it once and for all. This can be a minor change that only effects them, or a huge rewrite of the whole world. (See Marvel's <b>House Of M</b> for an example of the latter.)<br /> <br /> How do they respond? If they're suspicious, they're on the right track...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T21:02:39-07:00","id":916018,"title":"","content":"<b>Building a Better Tomorrow</b><br /> <br /> A shard has opened, and the shard is a fascinating one, to say the least. The supernatural is revealed, but instead of being a danger or sparking conflict it's accepted and a normal part of life. Vampires aid in medical testing by expertly analyzing blood samples and as changeling dream-divers act as licensed therapists. Shapeshifters serve as a special operation division of many police departments sniffing out illegal drugs and magical objects as mage orders act as fraternal organizations. Paranormal beings even hold public office, with several mayors either being werewolves, vampires, as prometheans make a living as semi-trailer drivers. Hell, the latest craze is the use of magical enchantments to put a coral reef in your own front yard to cultivate. Unfortunately, some wiseass kid mage decided to make magical jellyfish that infest them. Hunters, however, are the worst placed. While many conspiracies have carried over as official organizations under government control, many compacts and independent cells are seen as little more than hate groups.<br /> <br /> What happens if a character gets trapped in a world where their problems might be solved and replaced by dozens of new ones? And is it possible these hunter-terrorists might be this world's broken clock?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T17:35:28-07:00","id":916508,"title":"","content":"<b>Orion Trail [Infinite Macabre]</b><br /> <br /> You are one of those ambitious settlers blasting off to colonize a new world in the Orion cluster. Whether it is to escape persecution, persistent Huntsmen, or the wails of countless dead, or to seek new beginnings in more fertile hunting grounds or hospitable environments, you've pulled up all your stakes and committed to the journey. But it won't be easy. Stellar hazards and pirates aren't your only worries - even some of your fellow crew mates might hold secrets and dangers of their own.<br /> <br /> (Yes, Oregon Trail IN SPAAAAACE... and in the Chronicles are Darkness. Enjoy the Abyssal Dysentery.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T03:30:05-07:00","id":916756,"title":"","content":"<b>Lost and Found</b><br /> <br /> Strange equipment is recovered from the bottom of a lake. Research is taken to an abrupt halt when everyone in the laboratory disappears. Their families grieve, and are forced to continue living without answers. When the hardware is dismantled to gather dust in a warehouse it seems to be the end of the project. A small few never give up hope for closure and their persistence is rewarded when two decades later local analogue TVs begin receiving transmissions.<br /> <br /> Strange equipment is recovered from the bottom of a lake. Research leads to a catastrophe, as everyone in the building is replicated only for the two versions to haphazardly fuse with each other. Most don't survive the trauma. A few lucky ones are one surgery away from resuming their life - this time with a twin they never had. The Institute is torn by in-fighting concerning the future fate of the project. Many need to reshape their lives and provide some explanation to their families. Many require constant medical assistance to survive in their fused state. When evidence comes to light that the experiment created an unstable timeline and there is no way of telling which one is which, all work is directed towards making contact and restarting the project on the other side.<br /> <br /> It won't be easy. The technology is alien and prone to unforeseen effects. Both scientists and investors are divided about the right way to proceed. Survivors are faced with the fact that they have other families. The less scrupulous use the resources for their own purposes. Also, once the unstable timeline is determined, the world might face an evacuation on an unprecedented scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:50:13-07:00","id":916931,"title":"","content":"Hidden in the untamed wilds of the world and in the shadows of mankind's concrete prisons are the vines and flowers of the God-Tree, a gestalt consciousness of alien flora that dreams to reclaim the earth. It works through mortal servants and through its Angels, who hide the God-Trees countless Roots behind deceptive covers and far away from prying eyes. Its works push through the cracks of cities and sing beneath the soil of forests, conspiring to spread its spores and carpet everything in a sea of green.<br /> <br /> Stigmatic creatures and mortals in this world aren't touched by circuits and data, they sprout plant growths from their body and take on a photosynthetic hue. Infrastructure doesn't hum with the sounds of machinery, they're grown over with algae, moss, and kudzu. The Unchained of this Shard are still on the run, but face further unwanted attention as their human Covers degrade over time, unnatural fungi growing within them before bursting forth like horrific cordyceps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}